DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(sin(x))/6");
$fun_1 = Formula("sqrt((e^(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[1, 13] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, 4, 5}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -8, 4, 7, 8})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("({-6, 4, 5} - (({-9, -8, 4, 7, 8}) U {-9, -8, 4, 7, 8}))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-6, 4, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, 4, 5})) U {-9, -8, 4, 7, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[5, infinity) U {-8, 4, 6, 10} U [5, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("([5, infinity)) U ([5, infinity))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(3, 9) U (3, 9)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Lily had a long piece of ribbon that was [`17`] meters long. She needed to cut it into [`15`] equal pieces for her art project. After cutting, she found another single meter of ribbon in her craft box. What is the total length of ribbon she has now?

[_____]{2.13333333333}
[%
17/15+1

First, calculate the length of each piece from the long ribbon: 17 ÷ 15 ≈ 1.133333 meters. Then, add the extra meter found: 1.133333 + 1 = 2.133333 meters.
%]
---

Leo collected [`19`] seashells on Monday, [`6`] on Tuesday, and [`4`] on Wednesday. On Thursday, he decided to share his total collection equally among his [`10`] friends. After giving them their share, how many seashells did Leo have left?

[_____]{27.1}
[%
19+6+4-19/10

First, calculate the total seashells collected: 19 + 6 + 4 = 29 seashells. Then, calculate how many he gave to each friend: 19 ÷ 10 = 1.9 seashells per friend (using Monday's count as the share). Finally, subtract this amount from the total: 29 - 1.9 = 27.1 seashells left.
%]
---

For a school baking project, Sarah needed to measure ingredients. One recipe required [`9`] cups of flour to be divided equally among [`13`] batches. Another recipe required [`11`] cups of sugar to be divided equally among [`7`] batches. If she makes one batch from each recipe, what is the total amount of flour and sugar she needs for those two single batches?

[_____]{2.26373626374}
[%
9/13+11/7

First, calculate the flour for one batch: 9 ÷ 13 ≈ 0.692308 cups. Then, calculate the sugar for one batch: 11 ÷ 7 ≈ 1.571429 cups. Finally, add the amounts for the two single batches: 0.692308 + 1.571429 ≈ 2.263737 cups.
%]
---

During a school book fair, Mia had saved [`14`] dollars. She found a special offer where she could buy [`5`] bookmarks for [`17`] dollars. She decided to buy just one bookmark's worth of the offer. How much money does she have in total now?

[_____]{14.2941176471}
[%
14+5/17

First, calculate the cost of one bookmark from the offer: 5 ÷ 17 ≈ 0.294118 dollars. This is the amount she spent. Then, add this cost to her original savings: 14 + 0.294118 = 14.294118 dollars.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 3 < x < 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, 4, 6, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(C) \cup (C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, 4, 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -8, 4, 7, 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A - ((B) \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(A \cap A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -10, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, -4, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -4, -7>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10, -5>") x Compute("<9, -4, -7>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -4, -7>") x Compute("<-6, -10, -5>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, -8, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, -2, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 5, -4, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-10, -2, -5>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-10, -2, -5>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, -2, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, -8, -8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
